{"name":"Escarpment","hex":"#d5b79b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"escarpment","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A steep descent or declivity; steep face or edge of a ridge; ground about a fortified place, cut away nearly vertically to prevent hostile approach."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/escarpment"}],"entries":[{"title":"Escarpment","blocks":[{"text":"An escarpment is a steep slope or long cliff that forms as a result of faulting or erosion and separates two relatively level areas having different elevations."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Cuesta_-_Lookout_Mountain%2C_Georgia.png/330px-Cuesta_-_Lookout_Mountain%2C_Georgia.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Escarpment"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"escarpment":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/27/En-us-escarpment.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/2/27/En-us-escarpment.ogg/En-us-escarpment.ogg.mp3"}]}}}